\item use an existing \verb{<cid>_trimIDs.csv} unchanged;
\item truncate no tracks;
\item stop.
}

With \code{review = FALSE}, the \code{trimIDs} file already set in the config file is
used, or no track is truncated if none is set. Use it to repeat a run with
the recorded config file and track truncation file.

Records. Each run writes:
\enumerate{
\item the config file as used;
\item \verb{<cid>_trimIDs.csv} (if any track is truncated);
\item \verb{qc/diag/<cid>_dm_log.txt}, appended on each run, with the ArgosQC and
aniMotum versions (and git commits where available), the review
decision, the files zipped and the sftp outcome.
